{"nodes": [{"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_15_databases_apis_and_full_stack_patterns_04fa_listen_notify_and_the_latency_floor_md", "label": "04fa-listen-notify-and-the-latency-floor.md", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "page", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/15-databases-apis-and-full-stack-patterns/04fa-listen-notify-and-the-latency-floor.md", "source_location": "L1", "frontmatter": {"title": "LISTEN/NOTIFY removes the polling latency floor because a notification fires at COMMIT of the very transaction that enqueued the job \u2014 but it is a hint with no replay, so it can only ever be an optimisation on top of polling, never a replacement for it", "sidebar_label": "04fa \u00b7 LISTEN/NOTIFY", "sidebar_position": "51", "description": "The transactional delivery rule that makes NOTIFY perfect for an outbox, the dedicated session it requires, the 8000-byte payload limit, the notification queue that can fail every commit in the database, and why polling stays."}}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_15_databases_apis_and_full_stack_patterns_04fa_listen_notify_and_the_latency_floor_rule_1_delivery_is_tied_to_commit_which_is_why_it_fits_an_outbox", "label": "Rule 1 \u2014 delivery is tied to `COMMIT`, which is why it fits an outbox", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/15-databases-apis-and-full-stack-patterns/04fa-listen-notify-and-the-latency-floor.md", "source_location": "L19"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_15_databases_apis_and_full_stack_patterns_04fa_listen_notify_and_the_latency_floor_rule_2_a_listener_needs_a_dedicated_long_lived_session", "label": "Rule 2 \u2014 a listener needs a dedicated, long-lived session", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/15-databases-apis-and-full-stack-patterns/04fa-listen-notify-and-the-latency-floor.md", "source_location": "L49"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_15_databases_apis_and_full_stac